From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Takashi Toyoshima <toyoshim@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 23:50:58 -0700
Subject: Enforce isolated_world_origin lock on CorsURLLoaderFactory

Previously, CorsURLLoaderFactory validated request_initiator against
request_initiator_origin_lock_, but did not bind or validate
request.isolated_world_origin against a specific origin lock when
ignore_isolated_world_origin was false. This could allow a compromised
renderer using a privileged factory to spoof arbitrary extension origins
via isolated_world_origin to bypass CORS/ORB or forge Sec- headers.

This CL introduces isolated_world_origin_lock in
network.mojom.URLLoaderFactoryParams and enforces origin locking:
1. In CorsURLLoaderFactory::IsValidRequest, if
   ignore_isolated_world_origin_ is true (normal web page factories),
   any provided request.isolated_world_origin is normalized to nullopt,
   ensuring downstream checks (e.g. ShouldAllowUnsafeHeaders) and
   CorsURLLoader cannot be spoofed.
2. If ignore_isolated_world_origin_ is false (privileged isolated world
   factories), any non-empty request.isolated_world_origin must match
   isolated_world_origin_lock_. A mismatch from a renderer process
   triggers mojo::ReportBadMessage.
3. Guarded by the kEnforceIsolatedWorldOriginLock kill-switch feature.

Bug: 554038924
Change-Id: Ie6f3f7f6837428df66cb13f2fc1cb5982e4dd89c
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8402138
Reviewed-by: Kenichi Ishibashi <bashi@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Rakina Zata Amni <rakina@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Takashi Toyoshima <toyoshim@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698684}

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
features.cc/.h conflicted only on context (newer unrelated features
absent on this branch); only kEnforceIsolatedWorldOriginLock was added.
Unit test conflicts were resolved by keeping the branch's test code.
IsValidRequest() still takes a const ResourceRequest& on this branch (the
upstream constness change predates the fix but is not on M148); the
parameter was made non-const in the header and definition so the new
`request.isolated_world_origin = std::nullopt` reset compiles. Its only
caller already passes a mutable ResourceRequest.

